  "name": "rhdh-package-impact",
  "description": "Classifies whether an npm package in a Backstage-style plugins monorepo (rhdh-plugins / community-plugins, workspaces/<name>/) or the RHDH core repo (redhat-developer/rhdh, root yarn.lock) reaches shipped code (PLUGIN_PROD / CORE_PROD), plugin or core dev harnesses, local runners (plugins monorepo only), or workspace root (WORKSPACE_DEV). Discovers packages from open Dependabot alerts, classifies impact, checks first_patched_version, and bumps via yarn up -R. Use when assessing Dependabot alerts, CVE bumps on rhdh-plugins, community-plugins, or rhdh core, deciding if a CVE is runner-only vs shipped, or interactively closing Dependabot alerts.",
